<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-9899] Continuous query handlers are not called on backups when one-phase commit is used</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-9899</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Consider the following cache configuration:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Atomicity mode: Transactional&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Cache mode: Partitioned&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Backups: 1&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;If a continuous query is registered for such cache, then it&apos;s not processed on backup copies. It results in remote filters not being called on backups and lost events on changing topology.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Test case is attached:&#160;&lt;span class=&quot;nobr&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/attachment/12944104/12944104_CacheContinuousQueryTxBackupTest.java&quot; title=&quot;CacheContinuousQueryTxBackupTest.java attached to IGNITE-9899&quot;&gt;CacheContinuousQueryTxBackupTest.java&lt;sup&gt;&lt;img class=&quot;rendericon&quot; src=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/images/icons/link_attachment_7.gif&quot; height=&quot;7&quot; width=&quot;7&quot; align=&quot;absmiddle&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; border=&quot;0&quot;/&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
